# Requirements

This document describes the minimum and recommended requirements for developing applications with the Codexeron platform.

Meeting these requirements ensures the best compatibility, performance, and security.

---

# Minimum Requirements

| Component | Minimum Version |
|------------|-----------------|
| PHP | 8.3 |
| Composer | Latest Stable |
| Git | Latest Stable |
| HTTPS | Required |
| Internet Connection | Required |

---

# Recommended Requirements

For the best development experience, we recommend:

| Component | Recommended |
|------------|-------------|
| PHP | Latest Stable |
| Composer | Latest Stable |
| Git | Latest Stable |
| Visual Studio Code | Latest Version |
| PhpStorm | Latest Version |
| Postman | Latest Version |

---

# Supported Operating Systems

Development is officially supported on:

- Windows
- Linux
- macOS

---

# Supported Web Servers

Applications can be developed using:

- Apache
- Nginx
- Caddy

---

# Required PHP Extensions

The following PHP extensions should be enabled:

- cURL
- JSON
- OpenSSL
- mbstring
- fileinfo

Additional extensions may be required depending on your application.

---

# Network Requirements

Your environment should allow:

- HTTPS connections
- Secure TLS communication
- Outbound API requests
- DNS resolution

---

# Development Tools

Recommended tools:

- Visual Studio Code
- PhpStorm
- Git
- Composer
- Postman

---

# Browser Support

The Codexeron platform supports all modern browsers, including:

- Google Chrome
- Microsoft Edge
- Mozilla Firefox
- Safari

---

# Security Recommendations

To improve development security:

- Keep PHP updated.
- Keep Composer dependencies updated.
- Use HTTPS for all API communication.
- Protect API keys and credentials.
- Enable Two-Factor Authentication (2FA) when available.

---

# Performance Recommendations

For improved performance:

- Use the latest supported PHP version.
- Enable OPcache.
- Keep dependencies updated.
- Use persistent HTTPS connections where possible.

---

# Compatibility

Codexeron is designed to maintain backward compatibility whenever possible.

Breaking changes are introduced only in major releases and are documented in the release notes.

